<title>DENMARK: Danish ISS to run Norwegian care centre.</title>
<headline>Danish ISS to run Norwegian care centre.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish cleaning group International Service System A/S (ISS) said on Thursday its ISS Norway unit signed a 29 million Norwegian crown per year, six year contract to run a new care centre for the aged in Norway effective July 1, 1997.</p>
<p>ISS said it would carry out the entire day-to-day operation of the centre near Oslo, with the local authority maintaining ownership of the facility and selecting elderly patients to undergo treatment there.</p>
<p>-- Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
